 ## Background
-This method was introduced by [S1, unofficial] as an adaptive clustering approach for efficient triangulation of scattered data in the plane. It generalizes the concept of error-weighted splitting to quadratic polynomial approximations, offering an improvement over piecewise linear approximations for smooth surfaces. The approach is part of a broader framework for multiresolution modeling in scientific visualization, where hierarchical data structures are used to generate optimal approximations with triangles. The affine-invariant variant was discussed in relation to [102] (not cited in the provided source list).
